.TH CBMAP_REMOVE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cbmap_remove \- remove a key-value pair (type-inferred)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cbstmap.h>

ccol_retval_t cbmap_remove(hm_name, key);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Type-inferred wrapper for cbmap_delete_elem(). It returns the result code.
The map balances the tree again after the delete.

The lookup key goes through the DECLARED key type of the tree, in the
same way as in cbmap_insert(3). A key that the tree stored through that
conversion is only ever found again by a lookup that makes the same
one. A literal and a computed expression are both accepted.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
hm_name  BST map to remove from
key      Key to remove
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns ccol_success if the macro removes the key
Returns ccol_key_not_found if the key is not in the map
Returns ccol_invalid_args if key is a NULL character pointer, which is
not a string
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The macro does not stop the program on ccol_key_not_found
The macro frees the memory of the key and of the value
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_delete_elem (3),
.BR cbmap_insert (3)
